WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:21.030
This 1882 All-Star Game will be the best and the brightest as the American League takes on the National League at Olympic Stadium in Montreal.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:28.660
On this date in All-Star history, 39 years ago today, Shy Park was the scene of the first All-Star Game to be played at night.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:29.960
Bobby Doerr's Homer...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.280
won it for the American League.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.330
22 years ago today, Willie Mays returned to New York

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.350
for the first time since the Giants moved west

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.930
and homered off Whitey Ford.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.330
And 11 years ago today, Reggie Jackson

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.770
hit a towering drive into the Tiger Stadium lights

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.070
in the last game won by the American League.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.820
Beautiful Canadian sunset as you look down

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.120
from the Goodyear blimp, hovering high above Olympic Park,

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.880
the centerpiece of which is Olympic Stadium.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.900
And as we look inside, packed.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.300
to the gills. More than 59,000

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.180
to look on tonight. As for the

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.420
first time ever, the All-Star Game is

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.520
played outside the United States.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.460
Hello again, everyone. I'm Al Michaels, and

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.620
welcome to what should be a very special

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.680
evening as the All-Star Game

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.640
comes to Canada. They've waited for it

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.880
a long time, and what Abner Doubleday

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.540
hath wrought. He invented the game

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.360
in the 1800s in the United States.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.600
Now it's international in flavor.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.460
It's played in more than 77

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.420
countries. It's played by more than

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.980
300 million people.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.970
and it is the national pastime of more than 20 countries and what a marvelous

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.810
sight one of the world's most sophisticated cosmopolitan cities

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:44.000
Montreal built around a mountain Mount Royal the city deriving its name from

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.190
Mount Royal and let's pay a quick visit to Montreal Montreal is full of life

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.430
full of spirit while simultaneously maintaining its ties to the past of the

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:56.930
nearly three million people in the metropolitan area about two-thirds are of

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.550
French ancestry and speak the language.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.970
It's a bilingual city.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.100
and you don't have to let your imagination run wild

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.500
to pretend you're in Paris or Lyon or Strasbourg

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.220
when you wander the streets of the old section of Montreal.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.780
While rich in tradition,

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.960
Montreal is also very much in tune with the present.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.120
The metro is clean, quick, efficient,

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:16.080
and the modern-day architecture appropriately symbolizes

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.940
this country's financial and commercial center.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.930
When it comes to sports,

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.850
another symbol of the city has been the Montreal Canadiens.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.140
The names through the years have been legendary.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.500
Brichard, Bellevaux, and Geoffrayon,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.020
Plante, and Dryden.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:29.980
And it got to the...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.330
where the Stanley Cup nearly established permanent residency here in the summer of 1976 the new

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:41.490
outdoor stadium was the focus of world attention for two weeks when the Olympic Games were held

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:49.880
in Montreal the Queen of England was here for the start I declare open the Olympic Games of 1976

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:57.760
celebrating the 21st Olympiad of the modern era those were the Olympics of Nadia Koeman each

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.940
from the American boxers and of course Bruce Jenner who

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.060
celebrated his victory in this stadium in the decathlon in a way remembered by everyone.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.580
Baseball, too, has been an integral part of the Montreal sports scene,

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.320
and this present-day park was the site of the old Delormier Stadium,

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.540
home of the International League's Montreal Royals.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.720
In the 40s, they were a Brooklyn Dodger farm club,

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.820
and in 46, when Branch Rickey signed Jackie Robinson,

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.820
organized baseball's race barrier was finally broken.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.020
Robinson's start here that season went on to Brooklyn the next.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.960
The city went into the major leagues in 1969, and Jerry...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.960
Park, a toy-sized stadium, served as the home of the expansion Expos for eight seasons.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:40.500
The Expos moved into Olympic Stadium in 77 and have had a good deal of success here.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.800
But last October, a dramatic ninth-inning homer by the Dodgers' Rick Munday kept Montreal

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.760
out of the World Series for the first time ever.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.620
Disappointment that day, but exhilaration, anticipation, and excitement tonight for

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.180
the All-Star Game in Montreal.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.880
We're the part of Montreal tradition.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.060
is a very special lady Rachel Robinson Jackie's widow she's here with us tonight with Howard

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:13.190
Cosell Howard right so great to see you again and in this marvelous city which has such tender

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:20.530
memories for you and feel late husband would you capsulize in one anecdote the warmth of your

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:27.670
feelings for Montreal yes Howard I will say that when we arrived in Montreal and I has a 23 year

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:29.630
young woman had to go look for an apartment.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:36.090
approached a neighbor on DeGasby Street and she opened the door and she welcomed me, greeted

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:41.190
me warmly, told me to come in, granted me the apartment without any hint of discrimination.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:47.930
It was my first encounter with an atmosphere where there was no discrimination, where we

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:53.910
were totally supported warmly, and the love that we took from Montreal really sustained

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.510
us in the more difficult days when we didn't have that kind of support.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:59.870
And so coming home to Montreal to me

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.680
is coming back to really the birthplace of my belief in brotherhood.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:04.960
I really believe it can happen.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.520
Thank you so much. You've told it all.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:12.270
We're proud to have you here, and that's why so proud we all are

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.700
to be back at the home of the 76 Elements.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:17.080
Enjoy the game.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:21.580
I'll be back with a look at the method of selection of all-star teams.

