00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:29.890
controversy in connection with the all-star game are the right people really select

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:35.850
it and of course this year the focus of the controversy substitute Yankee

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:40.470
Bucky Dent until the very final days of the balloting leading the brilliant

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:46.090
Robin you out of Milwaukee to get a variety of opinions from the players on

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:50.980
how the team should be selected I went to some of them beginning with you out

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.460
asking him if an injustice was being done well I wasn't I wasn't sure if it

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:59.820
was injustice or not because to tell you the truth I don't know really who the

00:06:59.820 --> 00:06:59.980
Thank you.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.900
for if it's for the fans then maybe they should be the ones to pick the team but

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.900
if it's for the players and the media then you got to have a different way of

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:13.220
picking a team if you had your druthers how would you have the all-star team

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:19.000
selected well obviously I have to say the fan balloting is outstanding because

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.960
I was a top vote-getter but at the same token I would like to see it stay with

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.160
the fans but also include the players as well as the coaches and managers and I

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.640
I think in that regard it would be a fair all the way around.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.730
I don't think there's really a way you're going to stay away from controversy

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.490
because I remember we used to do it with the players voting,

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:40.880
but what happened in that situation is they do it like the second week of June

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.090
and the game will be played like the first or second week of July.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.870
And at that time of the season, there's a lot of players who have 180 to 200 at-bats

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:53.150
and if they go sour for a week and a half, they can drop 34 or 40 points in their bat and every.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:59.500
So the game's for the fans, and I think in most cases, the fans got the right starting lineups.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.260
That's why you have the substitutes.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:05.360
And me, for instance, if I was voting, I'd have voted for Al Oliver this year

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.420
because he's having a great year.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.200
You want to see the best players in the ballgame.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.520
It's just very unfortunate.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:12.280
Billy Martin made a statement the other day.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:16.540
Everybody that deserves to play in the All-Star game just cannot go.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.120
I think it should be left with the fans.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.440
I think the fans enjoy selecting All-Stars, enjoy selecting the players.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.860
It's the only opportunity that they do have to participate in the game.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.460
Fans are the ones that pay the majority of the salaries.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:29.980
they come to.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.080
the ballparks, and teams are successful economically

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:34.420
as long as they continue to pay,

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.080
as long as they continue to watch television.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:40.220
So consequently, I feel we should leave the voting with them

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.660
and for them to try to be a little more aware

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.560
of who is doing well at the time

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.920
so that ballplayers like Robin Yount and like Andre Thornton

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.720
do not get left off the All-Star team.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:53.480
For the final word, ladies and gentlemen,

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.180
Baseball Commissioner Bowie Kuhn, your comments, sir.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.980
Howard Reggie and Peter Wright, I like their answer.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.860
I think they're talking about the fans' game.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:04.040
This was conceived of as the fans' dream game.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.040
They should have playing who they want.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.380
If they want to pick up Pete Rose over Steve Garvey,

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.540
that's their option.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:12.280
It's their game.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.280
They ought to have what they want,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.820
and Pete Rose is right when he says

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.400
it's always been controversy,

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.160
will always be controversy,

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.180
and it does make a difference to the fans doing it

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.660
or the managers and coaches doing it,

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.050
and it's the fans' game.

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:24.030
They ought to have the vote.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.170
That's your opinion.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.790
Now, what's going to happen?

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.490
It's going to stay with the fans.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:30.900
Exactly so.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.110
Thank you very much, Commissioner.

