00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.340
Let's amplify more on what Howard was just talking about with the commissioner.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:58.020
Let's talk with the two men who have taken a great deal of abuse over the last few days

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.660
over the player selection process.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.380
players chosen for this first Tom Lasora manager of the Los Angeles Dodgers the

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:07.940
world champions and manager of the National League team tonight Tom there

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.880
was a time last week I thought there might be a lynching party coming from

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.780
San Diego that's right Keith they were looking at us from all cities and rightly

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:22.020
so because I felt that Tim Lawler and Jackie Clark and and Garber and Royce

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:28.700
and Guerrera and Bo Diaz and Matthews they all are all-star caliber and deserve to

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.700
be on the All-Star team.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:35.840
But unfortunately, what they don't realize is that you have to have representation from every team in the league,

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.460
and that constitutes the National League All-Stars.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:43.240
And when you pick somebody from a team, he may not be as well as another guy,

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:46.780
so consequently you can't pick that guy, and that's what makes it so difficult.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.570
All right, Billy Martin, manager of the Oakland A's and manager of the American League All-Stars tonight.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.310
How is it that we can solve the problem?

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:54.870
Well, I think we ought to have more players.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.610
I think they ought to raise the limit up to 35, and still you're going to get people complaining.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:12:59.970
It's a shame, but it's a nerve.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.540
and we have to pick the players like Tommy said

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:03.180
from each club.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.200
And you're always going to leave somebody out,

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.020
and I know Tommy feels the same way I do.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.220
He don't want to do it,

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.600
but whoever the manager's going to be

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.120
is going to get the same things being yelled at him.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.080
No way in the world you could play 35 though, Billy.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.120
No, there's no way, but they could be on the bench

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:17.380
and they could be represented there,

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:18.460
and I think they'd like that.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.560
Your ball club has only one shortstop,

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.180
two catchers, three first basemen.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.340
I'm a little curious as to why this particular

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.980
group of players were chosen.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.480
Is it that the American League folks are getting a little testy

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:29.980
about losing

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.360
Well, no, not really.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.000
We have the DH in our room.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.600
I've got two guys in the ball club right now that are DH hitters.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:38.740
They don't have the DH over there, so they don't have to pick a DH player.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.780
I have to pick players that can play out there.

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:44.620
So we have a rule now in this All-Star game that if my starting catcher gets hurt

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:48.480
and I take him out and put Parrish in there, I can bring the other guy back out there

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.420
so I can switch catchers once he's out of the ballgame.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.950
Gentlemen, good luck to you.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.450
It's an event where everybody's supposed to have a good time.

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:55.090
Tom, good luck.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:58.250
Well, thank you very much, and we're completely honored to be playing against Billy

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.490
and his American League All-Stars.

00:13:59.490 --> 00:13:59.830
Thank you.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.560
Thank you, Tommy. Thank you, Keith.

